family and neighbors coming out tonight  to remember a two-year-old hit and  killed at a park last night  they gathered at that park near lamb and  owens for a vigil  while remembering the boy people also  spoke about another issue they say they  fear will take another life  madison kimbrough joins us in studio  tonight with more  family and friends gathered tonight for  miguel angel morales  the two-year-old boy was hit and killed  last night while crossing the road  at a nearby park and police say the  driver was not speeding  but people who live in the neighborhood  are using the tragedy to shine light  on another issue they're dealing with  i've seen that little boy  a lot of times he'll be like a little  scooter  or something like that but he was never  alone it's just overwhelming that it  just happened so fast  two-year-old miguel angel morales was  killed monday night  after being hit by an suv while crossing  the road near douglas a shelby park  according to police the driver was  attempting to exit the park when the  child ran into the path  of her vehicle while speeding wasn't  determined to be a factor neighbors say  racing in the neighborhood is a big  problem  and they don't want to see another child  lose a life especially at night  like when the sun starts going down you  just start  hearing and seeing you know guys or  girls or whatever doing donuts here and  it's very dangerous because there's  always just like little kids in the  streets they speak through here like  it's a freeway  and you'll be looking like who in the  world will be doing that when there's  kids could be out here playing kids  could be running kids could be doing  anything a visual was held for miguel  where people laid out flowers  candles balloons and stuffed animals in  his honor  his mother maria morales who doesn't  speak english said she just wants  justice for her child neighbor and  family friend joanna aragon  rushed to the scene once she heard the  news she says she still can't get the  image  out of her head me and my husband run  over there and we just see the baby  on the floor he was he was really bad i  couldn't go to work  today i can't even sleep just it was a  trauma  and when officers arrived on scene they  found the little boy unresponsive  he was transported to the hospital where  he later died details about the woman  who hit him have yet to be released but  according to neighbors  the 19 year old lives in the  neighborhood now two gofundme pages have  been set up and we have both of those  links  up on our website reporting live in  studio madison kimbrough 8 news now
 

